    {
      "id": "2d5dd9c9-6443-4fb1-b95a-aa3d65568844",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1104,
        "content": "## Voice Clone\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow receives WhatsApp messages and routes them based on whether they are voice notes or text commands. Voice notes are downloaded, converted to MP3 through FreeConvert, submitted to Fish Audio to create a voice model, stored in Google Sheets, and confirmed back to the sender. Text messages containing the configured keyword trigger a sub-workflow that looks up the saved voice model, generates speech with Fish Audio, uploads the result to WhatsApp, and sends it back as an audio message.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure WhatsApp Cloud API credentials for the trigger and WhatsApp send/upload nodes, including the correct phone number ID and access token.\n- Configure Facebook Graph API access for retrieving and downloading incoming WhatsApp media.\n- Add FreeConvert API credentials and verify the conversion job, upload, status check, and download endpoints are using the correct API key and task names.\n- Configure Fish Audio credentials for both model creation and speech generation.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and set the spreadsheet/table columns used to store phone numbers, voice model IDs, and related voice metadata.\n- Ensure the Execute Workflow node points to the correct sub-workflow and that the sub-workflow input fields match the data passed from the main WhatsApp branch.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the keyword condition to control which text messages trigger voice generation, change the Google Sheets schema for storing voice profiles, or swap the conversion and voice-generation services if a different audio format or provider is preferred."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f3c40cc5-abde-405c-b325-60fa5e32e2ca",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
